{
  "_doc": [
    "Per-genre mixing defaults applied at MIDI export (midigen.audio.mix). Values are MIDI CC values 0-127:",
    "volume = CC7, pan = CC10 (0 hard left, 64 centre, 127 hard right), reverb = CC91 send, chorus = CC93 send.",
    "'default' is the generic fallback; a genre entry only lists what differs (merged per role, per key).",
    "A track's own spec volume scales the table volume relative to the role's spec default (so 'louder' edits still work);",
    "a spec pan other than 64 is treated as an explicit user choice and wins over the table.",
    "Extra tracks of the same role are spread around the role's pan (mirrored, then wider).",
    "'humanize' = playback-only jitter for rendered audio: timing_ms (+/-) and velocity (+/-). Taken as ~half of",
    "the midigen-genres groove.humanize ranges because the generator already humanizes the notes themselves.",
    "These numbers were tuned by MEASUREMENT (masking/level/stereo metrics of rendered audio), not by ear."
  ],
